            <ArticleTitle>Exercise treadmill test: estimating cardiovascular prognosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>424-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Abnormal hemodynamic responses to exercise treadmill testing may indicate an increased risk of coronary events and death, even if evidence of ischemia is absent. Exercise duration and the blood pressure, heart rate, and heart rhythm responses to exercise have prognostic significance.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
